WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.348 --> 00:00:04.100
- [Dominic] It's a rarity to
go to a rollerskating rink

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.267
and find live music there.

00:00:07.888 --> 00:00:10.207
- [Narrator] Most other roller
rinks have gone digital.

00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:11.941
But head to Southern California,

00:00:11.941 --> 00:00:14.160
and you'll find one of
the last remaining rinks

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.333
to employ a live organ player.

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.833
(funky music)

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:25.452
- My name is Dominic Cangelosi,

00:00:25.452 --> 00:00:28.285
and I own the Moonlight Rollerway.

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:33.717
I've been playing rollerskating
music for 70 years.

00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:35.850
There are only about 10 or 15

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.488
roller rink organists left in the country.

00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:42.703
In the ‘40s and ‘50s, most of
the rinks around the country

00:00:42.703 --> 00:00:44.535
used live organ music,

00:00:44.535 --> 00:00:47.239
and then when Elvis
Presley and the Beatles

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:49.978
all came into the picture
in the ‘50s and ‘60s,

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:51.561
most of the rinks around the country

00:00:51.561 --> 00:00:55.303
phased out the live organ
to play recorded music.

00:00:55.303 --> 00:00:57.904
- [Narrator] But not
the Moonlight Rollerway.

00:00:57.904 --> 00:01:00.102
Wednesday through Monday,
the Moonlight Rollerway

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:03.888
plays recorded music, just
like most roller rinks.

00:01:03.888 --> 00:01:05.758
But one day a week,
Dominic gets to dust off

00:01:05.758 --> 00:01:09.925
his Hammond organ, and throw
back to a different time.

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:13.497
(organ music)

00:01:13.497 --> 00:01:17.739
- [Dominic] On Tuesdays, I
play from 8 o’clock 'til 10:30.

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.464
The people that come on Tuesday
nights are a mixed crowd.

00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:23.097
A number of the skaters
are old-time skaters

00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:27.125
in their 70s and 80s who like
to skate to the organ music.

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:30.193
This place is special because
it's been here for so long.

00:01:30.193 --> 00:01:32.089
It's a historical landmark.

00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:34.123
People have skated here through the years,

00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:36.460
met their boyfriends, girlfriends here.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.921
Raised a family, bring
their grandchildren.

00:01:38.921 --> 00:01:40.381
And it's something from the past

00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:44.548
that I just want to hold on
to at least one night a week.

00:01:45.661 --> 00:01:48.369
I love coming here, I come every day.

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:50.129
And I enjoy my customers.

00:01:50.129 --> 00:01:54.211
They appreciate it and
they like the music.

00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:58.130
I have no plans to stop playing the organ.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.677
I'll play it as long as I'm here.

00:02:00.677 --> 00:02:03.740
Thank you for coming, and
hope to see you all real soon.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.573
Goodnight.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:12.195
(electronic tone)

